+// ---------- Stopping a game inside its host app (PadHub), so another can start without the app restarting ----------
+// A fresh boot runs the game clean: the game's own writable state is copied into guest memory at each boot, so only the host's own writable C state must go back to what it was at
+// load. Before any nxnative code runs (SwitchHubGame init calls dm_ios_snapshot first), this image's writable C sections are copied; the stop writes the copy back last, after every
+// thread has gone and every mapping has been returned. Objective-C, Swift, TLS, the dyld fixups and the host's const tables (swhle / swforce / swnvn) are left alone: they keep their
+// values across a run, and the runtime's own writes (selector uniquing, class realization) must not be undone
